From b5640b5344540b88028b6526add481a7ca1d4231 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MicroNUX contributors <micronux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:55:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/47] mmc: dw: use ESP32-P4 bounce for short aligned I/O

Generic DesignWare MMC sends transfers shorter than 16 bytes through PIO to
avoid DMA setup overhead.  ESP-Hosted's interrupt handler reads three 32-bit
registers with one 12-byte CMD53, and that PIO transfer does not complete on
the current ESP32-P4 integration.

The ESP32-P4 quirk already owns fixed SRAM descriptors and a bounce buffer,
so setup cost and cache ownership are deterministic.  Permit its word-aligned
short requests to use that path while retaining the generic threshold for all
other platforms.  Unaligned one-byte SDIO accesses continue to use PIO.

Signed-off-by: MicroNUX contributors <micronux@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
index 186e67a948cd..281f10db5b50 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
@@ -997,7 +997,8 @@ static int dw_mci_pre_dma_transfer(struct dw_mci *host,
 	 * non-word-aligned buffers or lengths. Also, we don't bother
 	 * with all the DMA setup overhead for short transfers.
 	 */
-	if (data->blocks * data->blksz < DW_MCI_DMA_THRESHOLD)
+	if (data->blocks * data->blksz < DW_MCI_DMA_THRESHOLD &&
+	    !(host->quirks & DW_MMC_QUIRK_ESP32P4_POLLED_IDMAC))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	if (data->blksz & 3)
